974. Subarray Sums divisible by k 
Leetcode link: https://leetcode.com/problems/subarray-sums-divisible-by-k/description/


Prefix sum:
Let prefixSum[i] be the sum of nums[0..i]. A subarray sum nums[i..j] can be computed as: sum(i..j)=prefixSum[j]−prefixSum[i−1]
Divisibility by k:
For the subarray sum to be divisible by k: (prefixSum[j]−prefixSum[i−1])%k==0
Which simplifies to: prefixSum[j]%k==prefixSum[i−1]%k
This means we just need to count how many previous prefix sums had the same remainder modulo k.

Implementation:
Use a hashmap to keep track of counts of each remainder.




/**
 * @param {number[]} nums
 * @param {number} k
 * @return {number}
 */
var subarraysDivByK = function(nums, k) {
    let count=0;
    let map=new Map();
    map.set(0,1);
    let prefixSum=0;
    for(let val of nums){
        prefixSum+=val;
        let rem = ((prefixSum % k) + k) % k;//to handle -ve numbers
        if(map.get(rem)){
            count+=map.get(rem);
            map.set(rem,map.get(rem)+1);
        }else{
            map.set(rem,1);
        }
    }
    return count;
};
